IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 2 -- Meaning of Act (ss 6 to 8).  Section 8 is repealed in the text.

§ `Part 2 -- Meaning of Act`

§§ `s 6 -- References to Act`

-- "Act means an Act of the Queensland Parliament, and includes (a) a British or New South Wales Act that is in force in Queensland;
-- and (b) an enactment of an earlier authority empowered to pass laws in Queensland that has received assent."
-- "Means" closes the definition: a thing that is none of the three is not an Act.
-- src:26 | (1) In an Act—
-- src:27 | Act means an Act of the Queensland Parliament, and includes—
-- src:28 | (a) a British or New South Wales Act that is in force in Queensland; and
-- src:29 | (b) an enactment of an earlier authority empowered to pass laws in Queensland that has received assent.
@ref s 6(1) (src:26-29)
GIVEN `it is an Act of the Queensland Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a British or New South Wales Act that is in force in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an enactment of an earlier authority empowered to pass laws in Queensland that has received assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a thing is an Act (s 6(1))` IS
    JUST (   `it is an Act of the Queensland Parliament`
          OR `it is a British or New South Wales Act that is in force in Queensland`
          OR `it is an enactment of an earlier authority empowered to pass laws in Queensland that has received assent`)

-- "In an Act, a reference to 'an Act' includes the Act in which the reference is."  "Includes" does not close the list.
-- src:30 | (2) In an Act, a reference to ‘an Act’ includes the Act in which the reference is.
@ref s 6(2) (src:30-30)
GIVEN `the Act is the Act in which the reference is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to an Act includes the Act in which the reference is (s 6(2))` IS
    IF `the Act is the Act in which the reference is` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 7 -- Act includes statutory instruments under Act etc.`

-- A reference to a law or a provision of a law includes a reference to the statutory instruments made or in force under it.
-- src:32 | (1) In an Act, a reference (either generally or specifically) to a law (including the Act), or a provision of a law (including the Act), includes a reference to the statutory instruments made or in force under the law or provision.
@ref s 7(1) (src:32-32)
GIVEN `the instrument is a statutory instrument made or in force under the law or provision referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a law or provision includes the statutory instruments under it (s 7(1))` IS
    IF `the instrument is a statutory instrument made or in force under the law or provision referred to` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- "In subsection (1), law includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory."
-- src:33 | (2) In subsection (1)—
-- src:34 | law includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory.
@ref s 7(2) (src:33-34)
GIVEN `the law is a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `law in s 7(1) includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory (s 7(2))` IS
    IF `the law is a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
